Several claims need correction. The oriented product gives a modulus square in general, while Kraus weights give an actual analytic square near zero. The mixed two-step block gives candidate zeros, subject to even-sector cancellation. Also, the single-layer supertrace series is trivial, but calling it a Berezinian would conflict with T1’s parity restriction.
